A||||5||ponya||seating front pads||||5||
Z||000000||ponya||01-23-2001||07:49 PM||||Just put two new rotors on the fronts and a new pair of brake pads. Problem is that the pads don't seem to be seating properly. They only seem to be catching half the rotor and I have a funny feeling in the pedal, like grinding without the noise. How long should it take for the pads to seat? Any suggestions appreciate. This brake problem is really getting to me. No matter what I do, they are just never "right"  Thanks to all,  Bob||||reg||5
Z||000001||MrPBody||01-23-2001||08:31 PM||||Instructions with my new pads call for 10 moderate stops from 30-40 mph with light pedal pressure (or something like that), and no panic stops for 200 miles.  They felt good after a few miles of city/suburban driving.<P>I have an '85.  What's yours?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||ponya||01-23-2001||09:30 PM||||I have an 86 SE. I've actually changed the whole system front to rear. You would think that the brakes would stop like it did when it left the factory. I can't even get the front brakes to seat properly. I might just have to concede and bring it to someone to look at it.   thanks, Bob||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||01-23-2001||10:48 PM||||Are you sure the brake calypers are on right?<P>------------------<BR> <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 01-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||01-23-2001||11:52 PM||||Sounds like:<P>A) The caliper slides are deformed or in need of lubrication. (the 'contact' edges of the caliper with the mount)<BR>B) The slid pins need new 'O' rings and lube.<BR>C) The outer pad is not seated to the caliper correctly (that's why I give them a "tap" with a hammer to get correct positioning.<BR>D) The pistons inside the calipers are hanging up. (get new calipers)||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||01-24-2001||07:42 PM||||any evidence that the pads are not running flat on the rotor indicates a brake problem. That or really crappy pads.<P>check all the things Indy said. Especially the slides and the pad position in the caliper.||||reg||1
